WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.220
- We watched another
episode of this show before,

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:04.440
but it's time to check out another episode

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:05.610
of "Body Bizarre."

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:06.690
Let's get started.

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:07.770
Pe-yoop!

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:09.330
- [Narrator] 56-year-old fisherman

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:13.830
and father of two Alejandro
Ramos goes by the name Willy.

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:17.460
Four years ago, Willy
suffered a horrifying accident

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:21.150
that mysteriously transformed his body.

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:22.170
- [Translator] I kept swelling.

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:24.300
My arms grew to an incredible size.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:25.380
It didn't go down.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:27.180
- He almost has the phenotype,

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:30.030
the body type of someone
who who injects synthol,

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:33.600
which is an artificial oil
made to enlarge your muscles,

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.670
but it's almost like not in his muscles.

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:39.870
- [Translator] I was working
at a depth of around 115 feet.

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:43.830
A cargo ship was coming,
it went over my air hose,

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:46.350
and cut my air hose in two.

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:49.560
I knew I had to surface fast,
I couldn't stay any longer.

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:52.620
I let go of my lead belt, and
got pushed up like a bullet.

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:54.690
I started to lose all of my senses.

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:57.000
I opened my eyes. Everything was blurry.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.790
- So the neurologic findings
that he's experiencing

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:01.680
is basically a diver's disease,

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:05.430
or bends, where basically,
nitrogen bubbles,

00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:07.740
part of the inert gases that you inhale

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:10.230
every time you take a
breath, start bubbling up.

00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:13.380
If you inhale those gases at
a depth of a hundred feet,

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:16.200
those gases are inhaled
at a higher pressure.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:19.890
Therefore, when you go into
a lower pressure environment,

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:21.600
those gases start bubbling up,

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:23.670
and imagine your blood starting to bubble.

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:25.380
It causes serious problems,

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:27.810
usually in the neurologic
system and your joints.

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:30.360
- [Narrator] Willy's
chest and arms ballooned,

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:32.970
leaving his torso swollen and deformed.

00:01:32.970 --> 00:01:36.450
- This is a very, very severe form of it.

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:39.750
Usually it's mild, and usually,

00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:42.390
it is treatable with a hundred
percent oxygen treatment,

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:44.100
usually in a hyperbaric chamber.

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:46.320
- [Narrator] Using a hyperbaric chamber,

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:49.710
doctors treat sufferers by
having them breathe oxygen

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:51.870
in this pressurized vessel.

00:01:51.870 --> 00:01:52.920
- [Translator] I've seen patients

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:54.870
who've had subaquatic illnesses,

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:57.420
and arrived completely swollen,

00:01:57.420 --> 00:01:59.430
but with the hyperbaric chamber,

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:02.220
these have disappeared
in one to three hours.

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:05.100
- Yeah, so he must have
had more severe damage

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:08.310
to his blood vessels as a
result of that swelling,

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:10.170
where it seems to have become permanent.

00:02:10.170 --> 00:02:12.330
And you know, when you
damage blood vessels,

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:14.640
and they become more permeable,

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:15.810
they could start to leak.

00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:17.970
When those blood vessels start to leak,

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:19.740
it could actually create edema

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:21.600
in the surrounding structures,

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.070
which is what he could be having.

00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:24.420
It's very similar to what happens

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:28.230
when you have age-related,
gravity-related swelling

00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:29.820
in your lower extremities, in your legs.

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:31.890
So you stand all day, you're age 60,

00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:34.080
your veins aren't as spry anymore,

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:35.850
so they're a little bit more swollen.

00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:38.220
Blood starts to pool
there throughout the day,

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:40.680
and as a result, they
become more permeable.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:42.510
More edema comes out, and as a result,

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:44.910
you have thicker ankles
at the end of a long day,

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:47.100
which is why we recommend
to pick your ankles up,

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.110
to wear supportive compression stockings,

00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:50.010
et cetera, et cetera.

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:52.290
- [Narrator] Willy has
had multiple sessions

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:54.150
in a hyperbaric chamber.

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:58.020
Sadly, he has not returned
to his normal size.

00:02:58.020 --> 00:03:01.140
As a result, Dr. Aguado
decided to draw blood

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:04.980
and take tissue samples from
Willy to solve the mystery.

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:05.910
- I wonder what part

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:08.220
of the body he's actually
taking samples from.

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:10.020
Is it from the blood vessel, the muscle,

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:11.970
the adipose fat tissue?

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:12.960
- [Narrator] A month later,

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:16.800
Dr. Aguado confirms that
Willy's condition was due

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:20.190
to nitrogen being lodged
in his fatty tissue.

00:03:20.190 --> 00:03:22.920
The next medical step
will be reconstructive

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:26.610
and cosmetic surgery to
remove the fatty deposits.

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:29.100
- How in the world do they need that test

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:30.127
in order to say,

00:03:30.127 --> 00:03:32.490
"Oh, get cosmetic surgery
and we'll fix it?"

00:03:32.490 --> 00:03:34.950
I'm pretty sure that would've
been anyone's recommendation,

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:37.590
whether or not they knew it
was from the nitrogen bubbles.

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:38.430
- [Narrator] Yulianna was born

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:40.980
with congenital melanocytic nevus,

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:43.290
a rare genetic skin condition,

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:47.280
that causes an overproduction
of skin pigmentation cells.

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:49.680
- And it not only produces melanin a lot,

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:53.340
it produces melanin a
lot in specific areas.

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:56.040
So as you can tell, it's
not her entire skin color.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:57.360
It's just sporadic.

00:03:57.360 --> 00:03:59.160
- [Narrator] Her
birthmarks and dark patches

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:03.270
of skin also made Yulianna
sad and self-conscious.

00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:04.350
- That's very understandable.

00:04:04.350 --> 00:04:05.790
If you're born,

00:04:05.790 --> 00:04:08.130
and you look different than
everyone else around you,

00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:10.980
especially as a child,
it's easy to get bullied,

00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:16.780
- [Narrator] Yulianna now
posts photos of herself

00:04:16.780 --> 00:04:19.570
on social media to promote awareness

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:22.660
of the issues faced by
people with skin conditions.

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:25.180
- I think that's great
in order to highlight

00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:28.330
that humans come in all
different shape, sizes, colors,

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:31.720
and just because her appearance
outwardly looks different,

00:04:31.720 --> 00:04:33.940
it shouldn't stop her
from living a full life,

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:34.930
and it shouldn't stop you

00:04:34.930 --> 00:04:36.640
from interacting with someone like this.

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:38.080
- [Narrator] One out of 10 people

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:42.070
with congenital melanocytic
nevus will develop skin cancer.

00:04:42.070 --> 00:04:44.590
- So basically when you have a type

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:46.360
of birthmark pop up like that,

00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:49.810
essentially you're having
micro-mutations in those areas,

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:51.760
because you're having excess production.

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:52.930
When you're having excess production,

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:55.540
that puts you at higher risk
for cancerous production.

00:04:55.540 --> 00:04:58.510
- If I will stay at the
sun for a long time,

00:04:58.510 --> 00:05:03.340
every of my small birthmarks
also can change to melanoma,

00:05:03.340 --> 00:05:04.990
and it's really a risk,

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:07.510
so that's why I need to go and check them.

00:05:07.510 --> 00:05:08.530
- The way that we check them is

00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:11.800
through a classification
system known as A, B, C, D, E.

00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:14.590
Each one represents a specific
criteria that we look at.

00:05:14.590 --> 00:05:19.060
A, asymmetry; B, the borders;
C, the color; D, the depth;

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:22.120
and E is evolving, basically
how it changes over time.

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:23.980
That's why if you ever have a mole

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:25.720
or birthmark that has changed,

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:27.640
that's a good reason for
you to go see the doctor.

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:31.060
And this allows us to
understand what risk each

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:34.150
of those birthmarks
poses to the individual.

00:05:34.150 --> 00:05:35.350
If some of them are suspicious,

00:05:35.350 --> 00:05:37.300
we do send them through a biopsy

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:39.610
to pathology to figure
out if they're cancerous.

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:41.200
- [Narrator] Dr. Watowski uses

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:45.730
cutting-edge digital dermoscopy
equipment to photograph all

00:05:45.730 --> 00:05:47.470
of Yulianna's birthmarks,

00:05:47.470 --> 00:05:50.650
capturing their exact positions and sizes,

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:53.140
so they can be monitored for any changes.

00:05:53.140 --> 00:05:56.830
- In her condition, it's a
lot harder to gauge changes,

00:05:56.830 --> 00:05:59.050
because there are so
many of these birthmarks.

00:05:59.050 --> 00:06:02.620
And also, look, if I
have two small birthmarks

00:06:02.620 --> 00:06:04.480
on my legs, and one of
them happens to change,

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:07.750
and we're concerned, we can
easily take that small biopsy.

00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:09.580
But imagine she has many of them,

00:06:09.580 --> 00:06:12.370
if she can't biopsy her entire skin layer,

00:06:12.370 --> 00:06:14.380
so for her, it's best to do this

00:06:14.380 --> 00:06:16.060
through a noninvasive method,

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:18.400
and be strict with it like a camera.

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:19.780
- This lesion is the only one

00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:21.353
on your body that it is
different from the rest,

00:06:21.353 --> 00:06:24.040
and it's a good idea to remove the lesion

00:06:24.040 --> 00:06:25.480
just for your own safety,

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:27.640
and then we'll assess
it with histopathology.

00:06:27.640 --> 00:06:30.130
- So histopathology is they'll
basically take a slice of it,

00:06:30.130 --> 00:06:31.840
look it under a microscope, and then,

00:06:31.840 --> 00:06:33.370
if they do in fact see a cancer,

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:36.790
you might have to go for
excision with wider margins.

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:38.080
When we say things like margins,

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:40.360
what we're actually saying
is that we wanna make sure

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:43.030
that at the borders of the
area that you biopsied,

00:06:43.030 --> 00:06:44.620
there's no residual cancer,

00:06:44.620 --> 00:06:46.540
which means that you
got the entire cancer.

