00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:47.890
- [Narrator] Joelison's astonishing height

00:07:47.890 --> 00:07:51.790
of seven foot nine makes him
the tallest man in Brazil.

00:07:51.790 --> 00:07:52.623
- Oh, wow.

00:07:52.623 --> 00:07:55.240
- [Narrator] Three years
ago, Joelison met Evem.

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:57.610
They weren't exactly a perfect match.

00:07:57.610 --> 00:07:59.710
Evem is just five feet tall.

00:07:59.710 --> 00:08:01.930
- Maybe that is a perfect match.

00:08:01.930 --> 00:08:04.390
Perfect match doesn't mean they
have to be the same height.

00:08:04.390 --> 00:08:06.610
- [Narrator] But there
was an instant attraction.

00:08:06.610 --> 00:08:07.900
- I'm instantly attracted

00:08:07.900 --> 00:08:09.580
to that little goat thing that they have.

00:08:09.580 --> 00:08:11.050
Is that a goat or a puppy?

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:12.100
- [Narrator] And the two were married

00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:13.510
within a year.
- Aw.

00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:16.090
I love that the cake
decor is true to size,

00:08:16.090 --> 00:08:17.470
at least true to proportion.

00:08:17.470 --> 00:08:18.910
- [Narrator] The couple is concerned

00:08:18.910 --> 00:08:21.490
that Joelison's fertility
has been affected

00:08:21.490 --> 00:08:22.360
by his condition.

00:08:22.360 --> 00:08:23.380
- It's important to note

00:08:23.380 --> 00:08:27.730
that before we start working
people up for infertility,

00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:31.630
we do give a substantial amount
of time to try and conceive,

00:08:31.630 --> 00:08:34.480
and sometimes that's a
year, or even longer.

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:36.610
- [Narrator] Gigantism
is caused by a tumor

00:08:36.610 --> 00:08:38.200
in the pituitary gland,

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:40.390
the part of the brain
that controls hormones.

00:08:40.390 --> 00:08:42.182
But by the time he was 21,

00:08:42.182 --> 00:08:44.680
Joelison had a range of
other health problems.

00:08:44.680 --> 00:08:48.370
He decided to have surgery
to try to prevent the tumor

00:08:48.370 --> 00:08:50.770
from causing further
problems as he got older.

00:08:50.770 --> 00:08:54.970
- I'm pretty sure Tony
Robbins has the same tumor,

00:08:54.970 --> 00:08:58.570
and was recommended by
doctors to remove said tumor,

00:08:58.570 --> 00:09:00.610
and declined, because
he enjoyed the advantage

00:09:00.610 --> 00:09:02.620
that it gave him, and I'm not his doctor,

00:09:02.620 --> 00:09:04.870
but I saw an interview with
him saying this directly.

00:09:04.870 --> 00:09:05.920
- [Narrator] Joelison will need

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:08.200
to provide a sample of his semen.

00:09:08.200 --> 00:09:10.630
- Basically, they're trying
to look at the number

00:09:10.630 --> 00:09:11.620
of sperm cells.

00:09:11.620 --> 00:09:13.750
They're trying to look
at the sperm motility,

00:09:13.750 --> 00:09:16.300
as well as other factors
to check if issues

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:20.140
with fertility stem from
something within his sex cells,

00:09:20.140 --> 00:09:21.460
or is it his partner's?

00:09:21.460 --> 00:09:22.570
- [Translator] Your spermagram test

00:09:22.570 --> 00:09:25.150
doesn't show the presence of sperm.

00:09:25.150 --> 00:09:26.230
- [Narrator] The excessive amount

00:09:26.230 --> 00:09:28.840
of hormones that triggers
gigantism can lead

00:09:28.840 --> 00:09:32.230
to a reduction in other
hormones, such as testosterone.

00:09:32.230 --> 00:09:36.010
This has led to Joelison having
underdeveloped testicles.

00:09:36.010 --> 00:09:38.500
- This should have also been elucidated

00:09:38.500 --> 00:09:39.610
on the physical exam.

00:09:39.610 --> 00:09:41.950
That should have been part
of all of this workup.

00:09:41.950 --> 00:09:45.280
I'm surprised that it took them
finding this out on a test,

00:09:45.280 --> 00:09:46.810
as opposed to a physical exam.

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:49.210
And I wonder if this
condition would be correctable

00:09:49.210 --> 00:09:51.160
by giving him hormone supplementation.

00:09:51.160 --> 00:09:52.840
- [Narrator] The couple
is now making plans

00:09:52.840 --> 00:09:54.598
to move forward with adoption.

00:09:54.598 --> 00:09:55.431
- Hm.

00:09:55.431 --> 00:09:57.133
- [Narrator] To complete their family.

00:09:57.133 --> 00:09:57.966
(Evem speaks in foreign language)

00:09:57.966 --> 00:10:00.490
- Oh, that's not a goat,
that's a puppy the whole time.

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:01.930
It looked kind of goat-y to me.

00:10:01.930 --> 00:10:03.670
- [Narrator] On the outskirts of the city,

00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:06.520
there's a boy living
with a unique condition:

00:10:06.520 --> 00:10:08.530
11-year-old Li Hang.

00:10:08.530 --> 00:10:12.280
Li Hang now weighs more than 300 pounds.

00:10:12.280 --> 00:10:15.160
He suffers from a rare genetic disorder

00:10:15.160 --> 00:10:16.397
called Prader-Willi syndrome.

00:10:16.397 --> 00:10:17.440
- Hm, Prader-Willi.

00:10:17.440 --> 00:10:18.340
You know, this is interesting,

00:10:18.340 --> 00:10:20.320
because this condition is
not something I've ever seen

00:10:20.320 --> 00:10:21.490
in my patients,

00:10:21.490 --> 00:10:24.160
but it is something that
is frequently tested

00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:27.010
in medical school, and on medical boards,

00:10:27.010 --> 00:10:28.900
where it's a congenital syndrome,

00:10:28.900 --> 00:10:31.630
where it's a chromosomal
issue, more specifically,

00:10:31.630 --> 00:10:35.950
it not only affects hunger,
but also cognitive impairment,

00:10:35.950 --> 00:10:39.160
sleep impairment, many other factors

00:10:39.160 --> 00:10:41.740
in the development
throughout a child's life.

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:43.210
- [Narrator] There's no known cure

00:10:43.210 --> 00:10:44.770
for Prader-Willi syndrome,

00:10:44.770 --> 00:10:47.710
which can also cause a
number of physical, mental,

00:10:47.710 --> 00:10:49.420
and behavioral problems.

00:10:49.420 --> 00:10:51.550
- His large size would
put him at higher risk

00:10:51.550 --> 00:10:53.320
for development of early onset,

00:10:53.320 --> 00:10:56.020
even, osteoarthritis, joint disease,

00:10:56.020 --> 00:10:58.360
- [Narrator] In a desperate
attempt to help him lose weight,

00:10:58.360 --> 00:11:00.070
Li Hang's parents are taking him

00:11:00.070 --> 00:11:04.000
to a hospital that practices
traditional Chinese medicine

00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:07.180
designed to help people battling obesity.

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:08.590
- [Translator] He has a
disorder in the feeding

00:11:08.590 --> 00:11:10.750
or satiety centers in the hypothalamus,

00:11:10.750 --> 00:11:12.040
located in the brain.

00:11:12.040 --> 00:11:14.650
- This is true, but it
it's a genetic issue,

00:11:14.650 --> 00:11:16.990
so it's at the core of his cells.

00:11:16.990 --> 00:11:19.750
- [Narrator] The medical
treatments here are unorthodox,

00:11:19.750 --> 00:11:22.960
but doctors are licensed
medical specialists,

00:11:22.960 --> 00:11:26.140
and the hospital claims
a high rate of success.

00:11:26.140 --> 00:11:28.090
- [Translator] We will use
traditional acupuncture,

00:11:28.090 --> 00:11:30.250
fire therapy, and fire cupping.

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:32.770
- This is where I kind of
start getting disconnected

00:11:32.770 --> 00:11:36.370
from the adjunctive
therapies, like acupuncture,

00:11:36.370 --> 00:11:39.160
where we're talking about
it for musculoskeletal uses,

00:11:39.160 --> 00:11:42.190
for pain uses, where there
seemed to be some evidence,

00:11:42.190 --> 00:11:45.940
and then we start moving it
to just general wellbeing,

00:11:45.940 --> 00:11:47.920
or obscure cases like this,

00:11:47.920 --> 00:11:50.110
where you're saying
that needles can impact

00:11:50.110 --> 00:11:51.670
the neurological structure

00:11:51.670 --> 00:11:53.770
and the genetic structure
of someone's brain.

00:11:53.770 --> 00:11:55.990
That seems to be a little bit too far out

00:11:55.990 --> 00:11:58.510
for me to say that it matches some level

00:11:58.510 --> 00:12:00.100
of evidence-based medicine.

00:12:00.100 --> 00:12:01.990
- [Translator] Fire therapy
with Chinese medicine

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:03.850
is where we incorporate extracts

00:12:03.850 --> 00:12:07.540
of herbal medicine that
helps speed up metabolism.

00:12:07.540 --> 00:12:09.820
We light up the medicine with fire.

00:12:09.820 --> 00:12:11.170
It is especially helpful

00:12:11.170 --> 00:12:13.780
for patients with abdominal obesity.

00:12:13.780 --> 00:12:15.700
- [Narrator] Finally,
Li Hang is given a round

00:12:15.700 --> 00:12:17.440
of fire cupping treatment.

00:12:17.440 --> 00:12:19.510
- I don't even know what
that fire therapy is.

00:12:19.510 --> 00:12:24.070
I'm not gonna lie, it seems
very non-evidence-based,

00:12:24.070 --> 00:12:26.650
and again, cupping, in general,

00:12:26.650 --> 00:12:28.480
has very weak evidence for it.

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:32.560
But then for myofascial
tightness, for restrictions,

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:34.150
again, musculoskeletal conditions,

00:12:34.150 --> 00:12:35.620
I could see it being valuable,

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:37.600
but for someone who's has a hunger issue

00:12:37.600 --> 00:12:39.070
from a genetic condition,

00:12:39.070 --> 00:12:41.290
it seems a little ridiculous
to treat it with this.

00:12:41.290 --> 00:12:42.550
- [Narrator] But the doctor points out

00:12:42.550 --> 00:12:45.160
that these traditional
remedies can only work

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:49.330
if Lee Hang is able to
stop his excessive eating.

00:12:49.330 --> 00:12:51.790
- If he stops his excessive eating,

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:54.850
he will lose weight
without those treatments.

00:12:54.850 --> 00:12:56.770
That's the core of the situation.

00:12:56.770 --> 00:12:59.350
So I find it ridiculous
that they're saying that.

00:12:59.350 --> 00:13:02.080
- [Narrator] There's no
foolproof scientific evidence

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:03.850
these procedures are effective.

00:13:03.850 --> 00:13:06.430
- This is where patients in situations

00:13:06.430 --> 00:13:07.750
like this are often misled,

00:13:07.750 --> 00:13:09.790
'cause they're just searching
for any type of cure.

00:13:09.790 --> 00:13:11.500
Where science doesn't have an answer,

00:13:11.500 --> 00:13:14.620
pseudoscience and
misinformation tends to thrive.

00:13:14.620 --> 00:13:16.690
- [Narrator] Marc may appear healthy,

00:13:16.690 --> 00:13:18.580
but he actually suffers

00:13:18.580 --> 00:13:21.670
from one of the world's rarest disorders.

00:13:21.670 --> 00:13:24.910
- Why is he looking at
the waters so angrily?

00:13:24.910 --> 00:13:26.890
I'm sure it has something
to do with water.

00:13:26.890 --> 00:13:31.540
- I have to drink 20 liters
water a day to stay alive.

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:36.160
I can last, without water, one
and a half, up to two hours.

00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:38.590
- I wonder if this is a
form of diabetes insipidus,

00:13:38.590 --> 00:13:41.260
where he actually is either lacking,

00:13:41.260 --> 00:13:44.530
or not responding to a specific hormone

00:13:44.530 --> 00:13:46.300
that prevents fluid loss,

00:13:46.300 --> 00:13:48.790
excessive fluid loss, through your urine.

00:13:48.790 --> 00:13:51.100
This is actually an important hormone

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:53.830
that your pituitary gland stores,

00:13:53.830 --> 00:13:55.810
and your hypothalamus creates,

00:13:55.810 --> 00:13:58.780
in order for you to be
able to balance the amount

00:13:58.780 --> 00:13:59.890
of water in your system.

00:13:59.890 --> 00:14:02.175
And that's a very tightly
controlled balance.

00:14:02.175 --> 00:14:06.790
- I will get very high
fever and dizziness,

00:14:06.790 --> 00:14:08.230
can't remember things,

00:14:08.230 --> 00:14:12.760
and I do not know in an extreme
where I am and who I am.

00:14:12.760 --> 00:14:15.850
- It essentially becomes
a form of dehydration.

00:14:15.850 --> 00:14:18.130
- [Narrator] Marc suffers
from the rare disorder

00:14:18.130 --> 00:14:21.400
known as renal diabetes insipidus,

00:14:21.400 --> 00:14:24.370
or nephrogenic diabetes insipidus.

00:14:24.370 --> 00:14:27.460
- The difference between
that and the cranial version

00:14:27.460 --> 00:14:28.930
of it is that the cranial version

00:14:28.930 --> 00:14:30.940
is your body doesn't produce the hormone,

00:14:30.940 --> 00:14:33.520
and in renal or nephrogenic is,

00:14:33.520 --> 00:14:35.770
for some reason, it's not
responsive to the hormone.

00:14:35.770 --> 00:14:40.210
- I wake up in the night,
and then I go to the toilet,

00:14:40.210 --> 00:14:42.460
and go back and sleep again.

00:14:42.460 --> 00:14:45.760
So you can say, okay,
maybe it's 20 times a day.

00:14:45.760 --> 00:14:47.980
- It's important that we point
out this has nothing to do

00:14:47.980 --> 00:14:51.730
with diabetes mellitus, which
is a sugar control condition,

00:14:51.730 --> 00:14:55.390
whereas this is a water
retention excretion condition,

00:14:55.390 --> 00:14:56.890
or a water balance condition.

00:14:56.890 --> 00:14:58.480
- Marc's condition is very interesting.

00:14:58.480 --> 00:15:00.010
It's a very rare condition.

00:15:00.010 --> 00:15:02.440
Unfortunately, we do not
have a very good treatment

00:15:02.440 --> 00:15:05.170
for those patients, not
to say we cannot cure it,

00:15:05.170 --> 00:15:08.050
but we don't even have
a reasonable treatment

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:09.070
for those patients.

00:15:09.070 --> 00:15:10.780
So what can I do for you today?

00:15:10.780 --> 00:15:12.887
- I love that the scene
goes from him saying,

00:15:12.887 --> 00:15:15.370
"We have no reasonable
treatment, we have no cure,

00:15:15.370 --> 00:15:16.690
but what can I do for you today?"

00:15:16.690 --> 00:15:18.040
- My GP?

00:15:18.040 --> 00:15:18.873
- [Prof. Spranger] Yeah.

00:15:18.873 --> 00:15:21.940
- And he found to tell me that diuretics

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:24.250
could be useful for me.

00:15:24.250 --> 00:15:26.020
- I believe thiazide class

00:15:26.020 --> 00:15:28.660
of diuretics can sometimes be useful here.

00:15:28.660 --> 00:15:31.570
- [Narrator] Diuretics normally
treat high blood pressure.

00:15:31.570 --> 00:15:33.580
- Well, not only high blood pressure.

00:15:33.580 --> 00:15:36.640
There are several indications
for what we use diuretics for.

00:15:36.640 --> 00:15:38.020
- [Narrator] Less salt in the body

00:15:38.020 --> 00:15:40.333
could reduce the urge to urinate.

00:15:41.320 --> 00:15:45.820
It's an experimental approach,
but Marc has nothing to lose.

00:15:45.820 --> 00:15:47.500
- And there's different
classes of diuretics.

00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:49.510
There's loop diuretics,

00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:53.320
which the most common one
that we talk about is Lasix.

00:15:53.320 --> 00:15:54.910
Thyazide-type diuretics,

00:15:54.910 --> 00:15:57.520
that are more commonly used
for blood pressure control,

00:15:57.520 --> 00:15:59.710
are chlorthalidone or hydrochlorothiazide.

00:15:59.710 --> 00:16:00.910
- [Narrator] After a few weeks,

00:16:00.910 --> 00:16:03.580
the diuretics seem to be working.

00:16:03.580 --> 00:16:05.560
Marc doesn't wake up in the night

00:16:05.560 --> 00:16:07.870
to go to the bathroom quite as often.

00:16:07.870 --> 00:16:09.430
He's less tired,

00:16:09.430 --> 00:16:13.540
and he has more energy to
pursue a very active lifestyle.

00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:15.940
- Always great to see
some treatments working,

00:16:15.940 --> 00:16:18.310
and I think that there's
definitely progress

00:16:18.310 --> 00:16:20.410
to be made in these conditions.

